Here are 5 places worth seeing in Jaipur, numbered on the map below. Hawa Mahal, City Palace and Jantar Mantar are close together, so they fit into one walk.

```a2ui
{"createSurface":{"surfaceId":"s1","catalogId":"foo.kit.v1"}}
{"updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"s1","components":[{"id":"root","component":"MapStops","stops":[{"name":"Amber Fort","lat":26.9855,"lng":75.8513,"note":"Hilltop fort north of the city, best visited in the morning"},{"name":"Nahargarh Fort","lat":26.9373,"lng":75.8155,"note":"Great views over the city at sunset"},{"name":"Hawa Mahal","lat":26.9239,"lng":75.8267,"note":"The pink 'Palace of Winds' facade"},{"name":"City Palace","lat":26.9258,"lng":75.8237,"note":"Royal palace with museums and courtyards"},{"name":"Jantar Mantar","lat":26.9247,"lng":75.8246,"note":"18th century stone observatory, right next to City Palace"}]}]}
```

India's real GDP growth over the last 5 full years swung from a **-5.8%** fall in FY 2020-21 to **9.7%** in FY 2021-22, and was **6.5%** in FY 2024-25. These are the official estimates as I know them, and the government revises them, so check the latest release before quoting them.

